00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.050
Could it be Isoletta's birthday?

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.780
Then could it be Vincent's birthday?

3
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:16.040
Arthur, what else could it be?

4
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.040
There seems to be a noise in the attic. Go check it out.

5
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.470
Alright.

6
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:28.470
Evelyn, gambling with your own life, is this why you went to such great length to drive Sophia out of the manor?

7
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.470
What are you trying to hide?

8
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.470
I'm sorry, Sir Vincent. I've used all my underground networks, but I still can't find any trace of Miss Evelyn's real past.

9
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:43.470
What do you mean? This is highly unusual. She has no parents, no relatives, no classmates. She's like an orphan.

10
00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:47.200
I think I know who she really is.

11
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:54.200
Evelyn, your anxiety and PTSD have gotten worse again. You can't keep staying in such a stressful environment.

12
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.200
My benefactor gave me a second chance at life. I can't let the murderer get away with it.

13
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.200
Be careful, Evelyn. Don't drive yourself to the edge.

14
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.200
Thank you, Doctor.
